// A *granted* module naming the primitive as a value. The grant admits the
// name (the domain is held), and what is left is the backend's half: a
// function value is not a call site, so no pattern check can be emitted, and
// the asm backend refuses the construct by name instead of emitting a `lea` of
// a symbol nothing defines. `BUG-k2Qv7` is filed for the C side, which still
// builds the function pointer the check cannot follow.
impl "util" caps(fs = ["/tmp/kelp_caps_raw_value_granted/**"])

fun main() {
    print(util.leak_raw())
}
